{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet","id":900708,"title":"Idea: Alternative(s) to Disquiet?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-26T22:42:40-07:00","id":900708,"title":"Idea: Alternative(s) to Disquiet?","content":"So I've been running a campaign for a while now with an idea that I got from reading through the Promethean books.<br /> I've read in the books that Promethean are sometime (often?) created almost like a relief valve when the world needs a particular type of hero. To Me that was a very interesting idea.<br /> Somewhere along the way that stuck with Me and I thought that Heroes shouldn't be creating nuclear deathlands around them for staying in one place for too long. But I soon came to an alternative to disquiet. I even had story reason for the change that allowed one to develop other versions of disquiet if that was fitting etc.<br /> So in My most prominent alternative to Disquiet or as we call it &quot;the D&quot;, was based off the Flaw (the name escapes Me atm?) that drew the supernatural to the player. This made sense. Heroes often get into the thick of it when they least expect it, and lets face it, sometimes it is not the Humans and mortals that need help, its the things that go bump in the night. Being that the campaign I run deals with a group of Hunters which not only work for mortals, but the supernatural, this worked out very nicely and also explained why the city itself was not dead wonderland. <br /> So looking into heroes, they tend to fall into all sorts of plots, schemes and often they came under fire from the humans around them if things stayed too ...comfortable without an en emy to bother the local populace. This sounded very close to what the current disquiet did with people not trusting them, or being jealous etc. So I quickly modified things so that more intense version of the flaw affected My Promethean character(s) and NPC's which took the Merit/condition. Because lets face it, not all Promethean are good guys. The flaw is optional, which explained why not all Promethean (or Unborn as they are sometimes called in the campaign) have it. It can be developed so that it gives certain bonus in exchange for certain increase in frequency or even appealing to certain types of supernatural phenomenon as well. <br /> I figured I would ask around and see if anyone else has worked with this kind of idea. Have you? *grins* Because the idea of a Hero is so important we even changed the name of the heroes from Beast: the Primordial to 'Champions' (lower case for regular ones and uppercase for the Apex Predators/Epic versions that would mirror Beasts) to distinguish them. Dont get Me wrong, its not that the BtP versions on heroes werent a great idea, but in a world of evil and EVIL(s) there is still a need for Heroes. In fact more so. <br /> With that, If you have ideas you would like to share, redesigns for these types of ideas, etc involving alternatives to disquiet that would allow players to stay in places while still impacting the immediate world around them that can be, fun, interesting and add multiple levels of horror to a campaign, I would love to hear them!<br /> Q: Wait, how is your version 'fun, interesting, and add horror' to your campaign? <br /> A: Well in My campaign Promethean would rid the world of evil(s), accomplish tasks similar to the way Qualishim or even Demon/Angel would. They would stumble into all sorts of plans, plots, and trouble areas. To ignore it would in a way increase the effect on the surrounding area in various ways, from more monsters coming into the area, to worse ones coming into the area, magic going awry in various ways, etc. Deal with the problem(s) and it lessens the pressure in the area. Sometimes even finding interesting ways to leave various energies (Azoth, pyros, etc), sometimes leaving clues, artifacts, gadgets and items needed to survive, adapt and move on should that be what was needed. And characters could feel when they were no longer needed, if the world was tying to push them out to a new location, etc. Its been working very well for the campaign, though the idea/thought has been brought up that they are a kind of supernatural sin eater for evil or bad situations that the universe/world needed them for. We seem to be ok with that, as they get to learn what humanity is about while defending it. A very good way to do just that. And in many movies, heroes are hated just as much as they are loved oft times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11556-coyoteschosen","name":"CoyotesChosen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11556_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T22:55:51-07:00","id":900714,"title":"","content":"What you're describing is a fine idea that has nothing to do with Promethean; without Disquiet, Wastelands, and the quest to become human, there's literally nothing left of the original game. You're better off building a fansplat about fated heroes than trying to crowbar Promethean into being something it isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T18:53:16-07:00","id":901622,"title":"","content":"I agree with parts of what you've said. Thank you for the fine idea compliment. Though I'm not sure that it has nothing to do with promethean. But to quote one of My players &quot;we just sorta treated it like one of the progressions like Aurum, in fact you if we slipped out of or changed to another path you had us return to using the disquiet table...&quot;. I dont agree with the &quot;there is nothing left of the original game&quot; comment, with things like pandorans in the game, however the idea to make something like a fan splat out of this track of thought maybe a way to do if one doesnt work it into a pathway of its own. But that being said, the idea to open ideas for alternatives to disquiet or how they function isnt a new one, the nuclear prometheans blast their landscapes differently. This was what was part of our groups original idea that disquiet could manifest in different ways to begin with and when discussed the idea that horrors showing up and the dealing with them could very well end up as an alternative to disquiet. It still can make a place unlivable, has a huge effect on mortals, even long lasting ones, etc. Though at the time I do believe Robocop and Batman were used to press the points, it still seamed like an interesting idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11556-coyoteschosen","name":"CoyotesChosen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11556_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T00:11:19-07:00","id":901830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoyotesChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=901622#post901622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with parts of what you've said. Thank you for the fine idea compliment. Though I'm not sure that it has nothing to do with promethean. But to quote one of My players &amp;quot;we just sorta treated it like one of the progressions like Aurum, in fact you if we slipped out of or changed to another path you had us return to using the disquiet table...&amp;quot;. I dont agree with the &amp;quot;there is nothing left of the original game&amp;quot; comment, with things like pandorans in the game, however the idea to make something like a fan splat out of this track of thought maybe a way to do if one doesnt work it into a pathway of its own. But that being said, the idea to open ideas for alternatives to disquiet or how they function isnt a new one, the nuclear prometheans blast their landscapes differently. This was what was part of our groups original idea that disquiet could manifest in different ways to begin with and when discussed the idea that horrors showing up and the dealing with them could very well end up as an alternative to disquiet. It still can make a place unlivable, has a huge effect on mortals, even long lasting ones, etc. Though at the time I do believe Robocop and Batman were used to press the points, it still seamed like an interesting idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be confusing Wasteland and Disquiet. Wasteland is the effect Prometheans have on the environment around them - the hellish radioactive wastes that the Zeka create, or how Osirans turn all water to stagnant, brackish muck - and that's been said to be either lessened or more variable in 2e. Disquiet is what the Created do to the mortals they spend too much time around, and I'm sure that's being tweaked in 2e as well.<br /> <br /> So again, you could totally do a story where your bunch of Prometheans on the Refinements of Aurum and Ferrum are compelled by Qashmallim and/or Fate to commit heroic deeds and deal with strangeness... but it would be something of a departure from the norm, and may well be better served with something else. <br /> <br /> You might try slapping together a new Refinement whose Wasteland manifests as a beacon to unpleasant supernatural forces (much like the Ulgan already do with spirits) and then explore what happens when you're both solving and creating problems, and the people around you really don't appreciate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T00:30:19-07:00","id":905445,"title":"","content":"I like this idea; it feels a lot more optimistic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=900714#post900714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you're describing is a fine idea that has nothing to do with Promethean; without Disquiet, Wastelands, and the quest to become human, there's literally nothing left of the original game. You're better off building a fansplat about fated heroes than trying to crowbar Promethean into being something it isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>This brings me to something I've been meaning to ask: What, exactly, do you believe is the core premise of Promethean? Having read <i>Frankenstein; or the Modern Prometheus</i>, I'm quite certain that Victor Frankenstein was a Transhumanist. He was literally seeking the means to transcend human limitations, namely mortality. The story of Pygmalion and Galatea never struck me as a tragedy. Osiris was still a god after his resurrection, and now had an even larger kingdom. I'm less familiar with Tammuz and Ulgan, but I DO know Tammuz is considered a god AFTER coming back from the dead. So why do some posters on this forum insist that P:tC be a game in which the core premise seems to be &quot;You're an abomination, the universe hates you, now hurry up and become human, so the rest of the things that go bump in the night can eat/control/violate/exploit you&quot;?<br /> <br /> And more importantly, why are those same posters so quick to scream that anyone not playing the game that way is &quot;doing it wrong&quot;? Why not play it that way at <u><i><b>YOUR</b></i></u> table, and let the rest of us play it how we want?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T01:00:59-07:00","id":905453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=905445#post905445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So why do some posters on this forum insist that P:tC be a game in which the core premise seems to be &amp;quot;You're an abomination, the universe hates you, now hurry up and become human, so the rest of the things that go bump in the night can eat/control/violate/exploit you?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's right there in the rulebook? The Refinements are there as guidelines on how to become human. Wastelands and Disquiet stress that you definitely aren't yet, with unpleasant and dangerous consequences. That is fundamentally what the game is, and all of the setting and rules are there to enforce that; the Created existence is that of the Pilgrimage and the journey to become human. It's like asking &quot;why does Humanity need to be in Vampire?&quot; or &quot;why do we have to be amnesiacs in Mummy?&quot; with just as simple an answer: that's what this game is, that's what the writers want it to be, and that's what the people who enjoy it enjoy it for.<br /> <br /> If you don't like that, you're welcome to do so, but Promethean remains the game that it is and 2e seems to be doubling down on the elements you dislike. I won't stop you from trying to crowbar it into a game that it firmly is not, and might instead suggest that you start from something more neutral and not actively loathed by you.<br /> <br /> tl;dr read my forum signature, I'm tired of this fucking debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T01:47:40-07:00","id":905479,"title":"","content":"I believe that one of the PtC2e blog posts addressed this very question. Something about the \u201cbuy-in\u201d.<br /> <br /> Bottom line: you're free to do whatever you want with the game; just be aware that if you try to make it into a transhumanist game, you'll be fighting the design of the game itself, since the humanist philosophy is baked into the game's essence. It's like trying to take the spiritualism out of Werewolf or the techgnosticism out of Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T02:02:44-07:00","id":905482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> tl;dr read my forum signature, I'm tired of this fucking debate. </div> </div> </div>My point being, if I want to take the parts of a gameline I like and downplay or ignore the parts that don't work for me, why should you tell me otherwise? I seem to recall the Golden Rule of gaming is &quot;If a rule makes the game less fun for you, don't use it&quot;. Maybe if your problem is reading how other players apply that to their <u>own</u> tables, consider that the solution might be to stay away from Houserule/Homebrew threads. Maybe the only winning move for you in this debate is not to debate something that you can't control, and that has no impact on how <u>YOU</u> play the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T06:36:15-07:00","id":905584,"title":"","content":"You're on the Promethean forum. Wherein other Promethean players are going to tell you what they think of your premise. Maybe they'll like it, maybe they won't. It's the price of putting something out there. If you look, nobody is saying you aren't allowed to do it, they're just laying out the reasons why <i>they</i> wouldn't do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T08:44:19-07:00","id":905672,"title":"","content":"And that's fine.... to a point. When mods have to step in and close threads because the &quot;YOU'RE ON FIRE!!&quot; players(Angry Villagers, as I like to think of them) make such a stink whenever someone even MENTIONS Transhumanism or alternative play options for a game that, lets face it, is one of the least popular among the 1e NWoD games, maybe it's time to put down the pitchforks and ask &quot;What makes P:tC fun and attractive to players, and what turns people off from it?&quot; I feel like maybe someone missed the point of the stories that INSPIRED P:tC, and now it's time to re-examine what the theme SHOULD be.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, can anyone point to ANYTHING from Mary Shelly indicating that peoples responses to the creature where based on something other than it's gruesome appearance?<br /> ANYTHING to imply Galatea and Pygmalion didn't live happily ever after?(Aside from being a Greek story, we all know how much they loved tragedies)<br /> ANYTHING to make me think Osiris went on a quest to become a mortal human?<br /> ANYTHING from these stories about these characters befouling the world just by being in it?<br /> <br /> No? Then maybe don't tell me those things are vital to a game based on those stories. Maybe the Devs were wrong. It's happened before...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T09:17:08-07:00","id":905700,"title":"","content":"Here's where we disconnect. I don't view Promethean as an extension of the stories you mention. Promethean is its own story, a Humanist story that inverts the approach of many other game lines, which uses references to the stories of Frankenstein, Tammuz, and the like as entry points for players. Even in the context of the game Prometheans have more in common with each other than they do with literal interpretations of their lineal creation myths. They use those stories in-character the same way we do out-of-character, as a tool to attempt to understand their condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T09:37:45-07:00","id":905712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=905672#post905672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the &quot;YOU'RE ON FIRE!!&quot; players(Angry Villagers, as I like to think of them)</div> </div> </div> </div>That you like to think of people who disagree with you in this manner speaks volumes about your perspective more than it offers any meaningful insight vis-a-vis the themes of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> make such a stink whenever someone even MENTIONS Transhumanism or alternative play options </div> </div> </div>You and I evidently have very different thresholds for what constitutes a simple &quot;mention.&quot;<br /> <br /> The &quot;transhumanist&quot; posters more frequently demonstrate a concern with downplaying or ignoring the aspects of the game that prevent them from having the Promethean condition be textually unconditionally awesome and assuming that humanity not having magical powers with which to stop monsters outright means their state is not worth attaining than they do actually engaging questions of how to improve humanity.<br /> <br /> The thread you're referencing was made by someone who continued to believe that the Created were naturally immortal despite being told multiple times that this was not the case and scoffed off the notion that the creation of a soul was an actual product of the Pilgrimage, which does not inspire confidence in their position's validity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:29:33-07:00","id":905751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=905445#post905445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm quite certain that Victor Frankenstein was a Transhumanist. He was literally seeking the means to transcend human limitations, namely mortality. The story of Pygmalion and Galatea never struck me as a tragedy. Osiris was still a god after his resurrection, and now had an even larger kingdom. I'm less familiar with Tammuz and Ulgan, but I DO know Tammuz is considered a god AFTER coming back from the dead.</div> </div> </div> </div> The good doctor is not a Promethean. He'd be closer to a mage - transhumanism is a theme in MtA, as is the creation of things that go wrong. The story of Pygmallion and Galatea, Osirus's / Tammuz's resurrection? These arent' the stories of about Galatea, Orisis or Tammuz. They are the stories of Pygmallion, Isis and Innana.<br /> <br /> PtC is a game about playing as the actual Creations. None of the previous stories are actually written from the perspective of the ones who came back to life as an effectively new person; even Mary Shelly's story is primarily from the perspective of Victor, and not the monster, and only briefly touches on the monster's thoughts and wants and needs. It doesn't describe any crisis of identity. It doesn't address the fact that they have completely different personalities than they did when alive beyond the most general sense. The stories end when their origins are complete. It'd be like if Spiderman's stories ended when he caught Uncle Bob's killer.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, despite tangentally using other stories, this is a Frankenstine story first and foremost. Galatea is not made from marble, the Golem is not made from clay. Everyone hates fire. And Promethean, as a game, revolves around <i>rejection</i>. Merry Shelley's story is a nod to her original rejection by her parents, and the effects it had on her as a child, and the struggles she went through. This idea is expanded in PtC. You are rejected by the land, by people and animals, by your very &quot;parent,&quot; and all the misery and torment that causes. This is the story of Elsa ala Frozen, who was told to conceal, don't feel, and all the pain that her family suffered because she was taught to reject very important parts of herself, and how eventually she came to terms with herself, and everyone was better off and happy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=905445#post905445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So why do some posters on this forum insist that P:tC be a game in which the core premise seems to be &quot;You're an abomination, the universe hates you, now hurry up and become human, so the rest of the things that go bump in the night can eat/control/violate/exploit you&quot;?<br /> <br /> And more importantly, why are those same posters so quick to scream that anyone not playing the game that way is &quot;doing it wrong&quot;? Why not play it that way at <u><i><b>YOUR</b></i></u> table, and let the rest of us play it how we want?</div> </div> </div> </div> Three main reasons:<br /> 1) Humans in the CofD are bad asses. Psychics, micro templates, hunter endowments are all shockingly powerful. The reason most mortals are prey is the result of ignorance. Someone that's in the know is pretty scary. Assuming you'd become prey is a stretch, and most such threads come off as hating on humanity more than anything else. That kind of attitude poisons threads as people react to the attitude.<br /> <br /> 2) Most of these kinds of threads ignore the main drive behind the New Dawn - get rid of Disquiet, Wastelands and Torment. To accept yourself and what you are, to find friends and family and a new life. If you're not addressing those major, fundamental points, then you are missing a huge chunk of the game, and the prime reason to seek the New Dawn. A New Dawn is an End Game. All problems and loose threads should be wrapped up. You can keep playing as a new type of game, but we're no longer dealing with a Promethean game at that point - you'd be better off with CofD core, or one of the other game lines. Being a Promethean sucks ass. Requiem Vampires are no longer the emo-whinners about how much their existance sucks. PtC is the one that takes that particular thread and runs with it.<br /> <br /> 3) Many threads show ignorance over the rules of the game. Focusing on Refinements as a new solution when refinements are meant to be switched is a prime offender. Another case is acting like a Centimani, or just leaving the Pilgrimage- things you can acomplish without the New Dawn, but are trying to be forced into becoming a New Dawn. Committing suicide is another. And few people enjoy being told their ideas are flawed, even if the criticism is constructive and points out ways to improve it. Things just go downhill from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-02-2016, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T11:18:08-07:00","id":905789,"title":"","content":"Well, why not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=905445#post905445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This brings me to something I've been meaning to ask: What, exactly, do you believe is the core premise of Promethean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if the First Edition core is to be believed, the Theme is Alienation and the Mood is Glimpses of the Grotesque. The rest of the introduction tells me that the core premise of the game is that all the powers in the world don't make up for belonging in your own skin and being a part of society, but what the fuck does Game Developer Bill Bridges know anyways, am I right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having read <i>Frankenstein; or the Modern Prometheus</i>, I'm quite certain that Victor Frankenstein was a Transhumanist. He was literally seeking the means to transcend human limitations, namely mortality. </div> </div> </div>Yes, and he is also portrayed as being deluded, the source of all his own tragedies, as well as many others, and ultimately a self-destructive man and a sad sack of shit. I wouldn't consider him a role model. The lens of Frankenstein, which is the lens we look at the other myths that go into Promethean, is a lens of <i>tragedy</i>.<br /> <br /> But hey, he's a transhumanist, so he's faultless, am I right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The story of Pygmalion and Galatea never struck me as a tragedy. </div> </div> </div>By itself, no, but in the context of our main lens borrowed from Frankenstein, it certainly becomes fucked up. But hey, additional context never made anything worse, am I right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Osiris was still a god after his resurrection, and now had an even larger kingdom. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but you don't even have to look at it with the Frankenstein lens to see how the holes imply some dark ass shit-you just have to hop over to Mummy the Curse and see how it skewers the entire subject. But what the fuck does Game Developer C.A. Sulieman know, am I right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm less familiar with Tammuz and Ulgan, but I DO know Tammuz is considered a god AFTER coming back from the dead. </div> </div> </div>Maybe people shouldn't comment on Tammuz until they've read the story of Innana's Descent into the underworld and understand that a)Tammuz was a god to begin with, b) Innana let him take her place in the underworld after determining he wasn't mourning enough for her, and c) He's a kind of Persephone and eternally torn between the heavens and the Underworld as a person, spending half his time in misery.<br /> <br /> But hey, he's a god, so it's all good, am I right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So why do some posters on this forum insist that P:tC be a game in which the core premise seems to be &quot;You're an abomination, the universe hates you, now hurry up and become human, so the rest of the things that go bump in the night can eat/control/violate/exploit you&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Disregarding the shallow interpretation, maybe we think that's the case because that's what the book says?<br /> <br /> But hey, you can't trust the source material you're working with ever, am I right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And more importantly, why are those same posters so quick to scream that anyone not playing the game that way is &quot;doing it wrong&quot;? Why not play it that way at <u><i><b>YOUR</b></i></u> table, and let the rest of us play it how we want? </div> </div> </div>Maybe because there comes a point where too much deviation from what the game means you're no longer playing the game, much like how if you slowly change a Cadillac into a Mustang it's no longer a Cadillac.<br /> <br /> But hey, none of that matters so long as people get to say &quot;Fuck you&quot; to humanism, am I right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's fine.... to a point. When mods have to step in and close threads because the &quot;YOU'RE ON FIRE!!&quot; players(Angry Villagers, as I like to think of them) make such a stink whenever someone even MENTIONS Transhumanism or alternative play options for a game that, lets face it, is one of the least popular among the 1e NWoD games, maybe it's time to put down the pitchforks and ask &quot;What makes P:tC fun and attractive to players, and what turns people off from it?&quot; </div> </div> </div>So much bullsh-Okay, we'll go through this.<br /> <br /> 1) Gee, maybe people say &quot;You're on Fire&quot; because the writers and developer have reinforced it as a highly pertienent metaphor for what's going on in the game, but hey, what the fuck do Eric Berg and Matthew McFarland know about the game they're working on, am I right?<br /> <br /> 2) Gee, it's like people have been pissing and moaning about how a game that was never designed to make an appeal to transhumanism should make an appeal to transhumanism ever since the game was released, but hey, what the fuck do people who actually get the god damn point the book is trying to make for about a decade know, am I right?<br /> <br /> 3) Gee, it's like the developers and writers wanted to do an experimental piece after the relative success of three major sub-franchises and were totally okay with it underperforming because of that success and because of that desire for artistic experimentation and were pleased to find it had a loyal niche fanbase, like the writers and developers have been saying for most of Promethean's run, but hey, popularity is the only thing that matters, am I right?<br /> <br /> 4) Gee, this would be reasonable if the majority of the people complaining about the game ever stopped to give due to credit to people liked the game and gave consideration to that in balance to their own desire, but hey, not enough transhumanism, so it's shit, am I right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like maybe someone missed the point of the stories that INSPIRED P:tC, and now it's time to re-examine what the theme SHOULD be. </div> </div> </div>Frankenstein was a tragedy about how the hubris of one man ruined himself and the life of his creation and almost assuredly set his creation on a path of misanthropy.<br /> The Golem is a tragedy about the hubris of a sorcerer trying to control forces more stronger than him and how his negligent attitude towards those forces resulted in murder and destruction.<br /> Wooden Tony is a tragedy about a boy who comes to so de-value humanity so much he becomes a lump of wood.<br /> Metamorphosis is a hodgepodge of collections that speak to the highs and lows of transformations, some as positives, some as tragedies.<br /> Stranger in a Strange Land is a tragedy about how a man doesn't understand people who should be kith and kin to him and ultimately dies at the hand of a mob as a result of his stark alienation.<br /> I, Robot is a critical look at the interaction of laws a created being must follow and where those laws produce strange and alien behavior, and what that means for humans who have thousands of laws they don't even recognize about themselves.<br /> Sin City is a Neo-Noir Crime comic about how one man's sympathetic pursuit destroys him in a city of people destroying themselves.<br /> Swamp Thing is a dark story about a monster on a spiritual journey to become human again.<br /> The Elephant Man is a tragedy about a person who is physically disfigured is rejected from humanity even though he is human simply because he doesn't look like what one would expect.<br /> Sling Blade is a tragedy about a man who is rejected from society for his mental disability even when he tried to do the right thing, and the problems of how his inability to understand people and they him led to his unfair exile.<br /> The Man Who Wasn't There is a tragedy about a man who ends up dying in an electric chair because one choice he made cascaded away from him, dragging his life through misery after misery to his death.<br /> A.I. is ...odd to place as a tragedy or a comedy, about a robot who's a boy who's obsessive love, childlike beliefs, and robotic nature leads to people questioning whether or not he is a boy or not, while his robot nature both gets him into trouble and out of trouble, and ends of him living a fantasy of just being a happy little boy with his mom for a day.<br /> Blade Runner is Blade Runner.<br /> <br /> But hey, all of that says to me this game needs to be more optimistic and transhumanist, am I right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bSo, can anyone point to ANYTHING from Mary Shelly indicating that peoples responses to the creature where based on something other than it's gruesome appearance?<br /> ANYTHING to imply Galatea and Pygmalion didn't live happily ever after?(Aside from being a Greek story, we all know how much they loved tragedies)<br /> ANYTHING to make me think Osiris went on a quest to become a mortal human?<br /> ANYTHING from these stories about these characters befouling the world just by being in it? </div> </div> </div>Gee, it's like things can be appropriated and reinterpreted to produce new and interesting angles on subjects. But hey, fidelity is the only thing that matters, am I right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No? Then maybe don't tell me those things are vital to a game based on those stories. Maybe the Devs were wrong. It's happened before.. </div> </div> </div>Gee, it's almost as though they were working on a canon of inspirations beyond the icons they used and listed it at the beginning of the book. But hey, who actually gives a shit what the real inspirations were, am I right? The people making their own books had no fucking clue what they really wanted to do, am I right? The fans who spring up only when Promethean gets a new release and not during the massive doldrum between the end of it's run and the announcement of Second Edition are the only sane and salient points of view that matter, am I right?<br /> <br /> Right?<br /> <br /> Look, I'll level with you. You don't like Promethean as is? Fine. I get that. It's a niche product in an already niche market. You think it can be improved, made more playable? Sure. Matthew McFarland agreed with you. He's spent a lot of time opening it up, loosening up some of the more restrictive gameplay, lightening the tone on a lot of subjects, so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> I'll continue to level with you. I don't know what it is about Promethean that attracts transhumanists. I don't know what draws you in, expecting some radically different experience. I don't know what keeps you all here when you find out it isn't, what makes so many of you fight to see Promethean become your vision.<br /> <br /> Maybe the problem isn't with the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-02-2016, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T12:51:09-07:00","id":905882,"title":"","content":"&quot;Why are people upset when I refuse the premise of the game?&quot; is an absurd argument to me.<br /> <br /> On a recent game design podcast I listen to, a developer talked about doing playtesting for his superhero game and one of his players said &quot;why do we have to play superheroes?&quot; That's the level of sense this discussion operates at, and at this point dragging the topic out of the mud for Yet Another Flamewar speaks to both a massive disconnect on the reader's behalf and possibly a deliberate desire to stir the pot.<br /> <br /> Promethean is the game that it is. Accept that, and move on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 06-02-2016, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T14:36:07-07:00","id":905962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=905700#post905700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's where we disconnect. I don't view Promethean as an extension of the stories you mention. Promethean is its own story, a Humanist story.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players\"> Challenging Human Supremacy in HtV Players - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/902486-challenging-human-supremacy-in-htv-players </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Whether the setting is fantasy or science fiction, if it involves humans meeting with non-humans, there is a sub-genre which, at least in the eyes of its fans, is dedicated to emphasizing the superiority and unquenchable moral rightness of humanity. On /tg/ boards, this motif is called &amp;quot;Humanity, Fuck Yeah!&amp;quot;, but to avoid getting banned by the mods for excessive swearing, I've gone for the hopefully less incendiary stand in of &amp;quot;human supremacy&amp;quot;. Now, human supremacists interested in the Chronicles of Darkness setting just love Hunter: The Vigil, seeing it as basically a celebration </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T15:09:38-07:00","id":905986,"title":"","content":"Hunter is not Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T15:24:27-07:00","id":906002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=905751#post905751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It'd be like if Spiderman's stories ended when he caught <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Uncle Bob's </span>killer.</div> </div> </div> </div> His name was Ben.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, despite tangentally using other stories, this is a Frankenstine story first and foremost. Galatea is not made from marble, the Golem is not made from clay. Everyone hates fire. And Promethean, as a game, revolves around <i>rejection</i>. Merry Shelley's story is a nod to her original rejection by her parents, and the effects it had on her as a child, and the struggles she went through. This idea is expanded in PtC. You are rejected by the land, by people and animals, by your very &quot;parent,&quot; and all the misery and torment that causes. This is the story of Elsa ala Frozen, who was told to conceal, don't feel, and all the pain that her family suffered because she was taught to reject very important parts of herself, and how eventually she came to terms with herself, and everyone was better off and happy. </div> </div> </div> We're almost on the same page. As you say, Elsa was happier when she learned to accept, and even celebrate, the things that made her Different. When a Promethean does the same thing, we call them a Centimani. If she had gone on a quest to rid herself of her magic, THAT would feel like what Promethean seems to insist is the ONLY answer.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason most mortals are prey is the result of ignorance. Someone that's in the know is pretty scary. </div> </div> </div> And if you mess up your Final Azoth roll, you wind up completely ignorant.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assuming you'd become prey is a stretch, and most such threads come off as hating on humanity more than anything else. That kind of attitude poisons threads as people react to the attitude. </div> </div> </div> You have a point there. Let me be clear, I don't hate humanity; I hate conformity. Sometimes the mutation is beneficial. I feel like exploring how being something different can be a good thing SHOULD be treated as a viable path in the game.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of these kinds of threads ignore the main drive behind the New Dawn - get rid of Disquiet, Wastelands and Torment. </div> </div> </div> Which is what I believe the OP intended for this thread; an alternative version of those drawbacks.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To accept yourself and what you are, to find friends and family and a new life. If you're not addressing those major, fundamental points, then you are missing a huge chunk of the game, and the prime reason to seek the New Dawn. A New Dawn is an End Game. All problems and loose threads should be wrapped up. </div> </div> </div> Again, &quot;Angry Villagers&quot; will tell you that NO, you CAN'T accept who/what you ARE, you have to become something/someone ELSE. I'd rather be able to change what I see wrong with the world.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And few people enjoy being told their ideas are flawed, even if the criticism is constructive and points out ways to improve it. Things just go downhill from there. </div> </div> </div> And there's the conflict between Humanists and Transhumanist players; the Humanists frequently show up in threads they KNOW are about an idea they don't like, and start ranting about how flawed the idea is.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:01:29-07:00","id":906029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=905986#post905986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter is not Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe point remains; &quot;Humans:Fuck Yeah!&quot; is pretty much what some of us get from Promethean 1e. I will concede that much of what I had posted last night was more emotional than rational, and therefore poorly worded. My contention is simply that it would have been nice if the Devs had considered some more of the POSITIVES about the stories they used as inspiration. There are a LOT of themes in Promethean that I love; and I want to play a game with those themes. Believe me, I know how frustrating it can be to have someone want to make something you love into something that you don't recognize; I'm a Marvel fan.(BTW, Swampthing was a plant that dreamed it was a man) But that doesn't mean I would begrudge someone taking ASPECTS of something I love, to make something new. So let me tell you the things I dig about Promethean:<br /> Resurrection. Due to a host of things I won't get into here, I have a serious issue with the idea of death being permanent.<br /> Alchemy. More the external kind than the internal, but internal can be interesting too. But to me, Refinement means working towards being the best possible version of who/what you ARE, not becoming a different person/thing. When you refine a metal, you still end up with the same metal, just purer, more true to itself.<br /> Elementalism. Not the BIGGEST theme in P:tC, but it's there.<br /> <br /> So, I think we ALL, myself included, have derailed this thread enough. I believe I know which inspiration the OP was drawing from when he proposed the &quot;Prometheans as misunderstood heroes/created for a purpose&quot; idea; The Crow is listed as an inspiration.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:16:21-07:00","id":906039,"title":"","content":"While there's a lot of exaggeration on both sides, &quot;Humans, Fuck Yeah!&quot; is not an inappropriate response for a Humanist game, considering that it's bottom line is essentially that.<br /> <br /> And that's the heart of the problem. It has been established, time after time after time after time after time after time after time after time after after time, again and again and again and again and again and again and again and again and again and again, that this is a more experimental art-piece gameline about humanism, and people keep going on about it, some ruder than others. And the elements that fuel and direct and make this game distinct in it's humanism are the same things people want to change. It's wanting to change the the things that make Promethean <i>Promethean</i>.<br /> <br /> Not all games are for all people. They can't be. They <i>shouldn't</i> be. And I think after a decade, it should be clear who Promethean is and isn't for.<br /> <br /> I apologize about getting heated, and I appreciate you sharing what appeals to you. But there are points Promethean can't compromise on, and after <i>ten years</i> of people fighting to make it do that, patience is hard to hold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-02-2016, 05:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:25:09-07:00","id":906043,"title":"","content":"Promethean: the Created; not Promethean: Resurrection. And transmuting metals <i>is</i> about changing from one metal to another: \u201cfrom Lead to Gold\u201d, remember? <br /> <br /> Also, I suspect you wouldn't have gotten the firestorm of responses you got if you hadn't been characterizing posters as \u201ctorch-wielding mobs\u201d and the like. Arc has apologized for getting heated; maybe an apology for trolling (unintentionally, I hope) is also in order?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T16:29:40-07:00","id":906044,"title":"","content":"On a different note, I can't help someone if their main problem is the fact that Disquiet and Wasteland don't seem like fun problems to work with(I'm a sado-masochist, so go figure I do), but if people want a transhumanist angle on the game, I always figured the answer was easy-when you Redeem, you lose Disquiet, Wasteland, Torment, and Disfigurements. Keep the positives. It doesn't make metaphysical sense, but screw it. That way you keep in the journey, can explore and learn about humanity anyways, take the good you have and add to it, and end up as a transhumanist wet dream, monster or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T17:34:54-07:00","id":906073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906002#post906002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're almost on the same page. As you say, Elsa was happier when she learned to accept, and even celebrate, the things that made her Different. When a Promethean does the same thing, we call them a Centimani. If she had gone on a quest to rid herself of her magic, THAT would feel like what Promethean seems to insist is the ONLY answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always felt this created unfortunate implications for the gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T17:54:00-07:00","id":906086,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't buy the Elsa analogy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T18:01:07-07:00","id":906090,"title":"","content":"The thing about Prometheans is that they are not born. They are (wait for it) <i>created</i>. Even moreso than every other flesh blob on our poor damned space rock they are trapped in an existence they never asked for, doing the best that they can with a suite of shitty options. Its important to realize that the New Dawn isn't just a pipe-dream. It is one hundred percent achievable and maintaining hope in the face of long odds is a core part of the game (isn't Elpis going to be their Integrity stat in 2E?). Moreover, they are <i>incomplete</i> creations. A flawed being made in the image of an equally flawed being. You have every right to hate your creator for that, you have every right to hate the shitty world you were put into and the even-shittier-than-normal hand you were dealt, you have every right to hate the Principle and the Pilgrimage and every damned thing about it. None of them can fix it for you though, only <i>you</i> can do that. <br /> <br /> By making the purpose of the Pilgrimage becoming human Promethean becomes a conversation about what being human <i>is</i>. It doesn't give you an easy path or clear answers because both of those would be ultimately incorrect. It is the journey of getting there, of the debate and conversation, that makes Promethean what it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T18:49:36-07:00","id":906115,"title":"","content":"\u201cPilgrimage\u201d is the 2e Integrity substitute. \u201cElpis\u201d is still a Merit. <br /> <br /> IMHO, the Elsa analogy is a better fit for Beast. That's a game that's very much about celebrating being on the outs with humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T19:31:11-07:00","id":906134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906002#post906002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're almost on the same page. As you say, Elsa was happier when she learned to accept, and even celebrate, the things that made her Different. When a Promethean does the same thing, we call them a Centimani. If she had gone on a quest to rid herself of her magic, THAT would feel like what Promethean seems to insist is the ONLY answer.</div> </div> </div> </div> *Shrugs* Which is why I support doing things like become another supernatural or psychic, or keeping Transmutations. In fact, I did it back in 1e. No one really cared, though, because it was post New Dawn, and the game's basically over at that point.<br /> <br /> In fact, when I described what I did online, no one cared one whit. No one cares really about the final outcome, so long as it maintains the themes of the game. And that's the problem - most of the proposed hacks don't. That's why the bile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you mess up your Final Azoth roll, you wind up completely ignorant. </div> </div> </div> Simple enough hack in 1e, and not true in 2e. I subscribe to the thought that a roll shouldn't determine the success of your New Dawn in the first place, and found that entire idea wacky. Dramatic moments shouldn't be subject to the whims of the dice. And, again, no one really cared about hacking that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have a point there. Let me be clear, I don't hate humanity; I hate conformity. Sometimes the mutation is beneficial. I feel like exploring how being something different can be a good thing SHOULD be treated as a viable path in the game. </div> </div> </div> Lots of people have that misunderstanding. I know several of the LGTBQIA+ community felt the game was tell them to conform to &quot;standard&quot; humanity, when I don't think that was the goal of the game. And, to be honest, if we have a significant number of people with that misunderstanding, that's a failure of the material, not the people. I don't know if the people who interpreted the game that way are a significant or not, because its unavoidable that a small handful will misunderstand. In any case, that's beyond the scope of this discussion.<br /> <br /> To use an that LGBT example, I think that the Pilgrimage is about suffering hate because of sexual inclinations, lashing out in anger or depraved sexuality that hurts you, or whatever. Its about people talking about you behind your back and pointing fingers. And then, the New Dawn is about achieving balance, finding where you belong, where you can find people that will love you for who you are, and will accept you, Its about letting go of the anger and hurt.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I'd also like to point out that conformity as a method of control and Tyranny is one of the central conflicts of the Seers of the Throne.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is what I believe the OP intended for this thread; an alternative version of those drawbacks. </div> </div> </div> The OP wanted to portray Prometheans as heroes. While its possible for individuals to be heroic, in general, that's not the point of the CofD. The OP is attempting to hack the game into something completely different to the point most of us wouldn't recognize the game anymore.<br /> <br /> And, you know what? That's fine if they have fun. But its an uphill battle that most of us aren't comfortable engaging in and making rules for. Its like removing paradox and obsessions from Mage, or making all vampires into superheroes with fangs instead of monsters. It destroys what most of us are interested in. At best, we can report how we feel on the issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, &quot;Angry Villagers&quot; will tell you that NO, you CAN'T accept who/what you ARE, you have to become something/someone ELSE. I'd rather be able to change what I see wrong with the world. </div> </div> </div> Promethean isn't about changing the world. Promethean is about changing the way you see the world and finding your place in it. This is where things get heated - Promethean is a very &quot;internal&quot; game. Its about seeking personal understanding and enlightenment.<br /> <br /> No one is arguing against accepting yourself. They're arguing against someone with genuine mental issues not getting treatment for them. They're arguing against someone with a medical condition that literally poisons the world around them being happy about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And there's the conflict between Humanists and Transhumanist players; the Humanists frequently show up in threads they KNOW are about an idea they don't like, and start ranting about how flawed the idea is. </div> </div> </div> That's a false dichotomy. This isn't about transhumanism versus humanism. It never was. That's merely a flag people wave to justify their ideas. Transhumanity is the belief humans can use science to evolve past <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">its current physical and mental limitations. The ideas most posters present never address the fundamental limitations of the Promethean condition, only focusing on expanding more powers. Transhumanity isn't about leaving those of us mentally ill behind. Or embracing mentally imbalanced, or anything like that.<br /> <br /> The central issue is that most of the people in the &quot;humanist&quot; camp, as you put it, find these examples of so-called &quot;transhumanism&quot; to be horrifying monsters <i>more </i>screwed over than a regular prommie on the Pilgrimage. That's why most people accuse these alternate New Dawn threads of being just glorified Centimani - because these threads are often about getting more powers without mitigating any of the problems.</span></span><br /> <br /> I know of at least twice in the past that people who claimed to be transhumanists mocking the Promethean mental disorders. True transhumanity cares about mental issues and seeks to overcome them.<br /> <br /> Just take a look at Arcane's post a few above. Get rid of the drawbacks, keep the Transmutations and powers. And done. That's a very transhumanist suggestion right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-02-2016, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T21:02:42-07:00","id":906179,"title":"","content":"To be fair, that's not entirely true. A lot of the \u201calternate dawns\u201d stuff is explicitly about getting rid of the drawbacks of being a Promethean. It seems to me that if that's what you're looking for, VtR's Ordo Dracul and their Coils of the Dragon are more up your alley. And IIRC, the Plumbum Refinement is likewise geared toward mitigating a Promethean's downsides. <br /> <br /> The reason why I wouldn't use most of these variants is that they take a dump on the notion that becoming human is a worthwhile goal. I don't mind alternatives; but most of them start with the premise that Promethean's natural themes are stupid. Note @Mangle77's characterization of the New Dawn from his first post in this thread: <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">\u201cnow hurry up and become human, so the rest of the things that go bump in the night can eat/control/violate/exploit you.\u201d</span> The implication there is that no one in their right mind would want to become human; so we need to find alternatives to <b>Promethean</b>'s standard design that <i>make sense</i>, by making the Promethean condition not suck so much and/or by replacing the end goal with something that doesn't suck so much. <br /> <br /> <i>That's</i> what bothers me about most of the so-called \u201ctranshumanist\u201d hacks I've seen on this forum: they're not about providing alternate takes on <b>Promethean</b>; they're about rewriting it into something incompatible with what <b>Promethean</b> was intended to be. No, not just \u201cincompatible\u201d; something designed to refute and undermine the intent of the game. So-called \u201calternate\u201d New Dawns aren't designed to exist alongside \u201cbecoming human\u201d; they're designed to render \u201cbecoming human\u201d moot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-03-2016, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T01:37:51-07:00","id":906282,"title":"","content":"So, I'm not going to quote everyone, but let me respond to some of this. You are correct; I let my feelings get the best of me, and became overly confrontational, and for that I apologize. I've been told I'm somewhere on the Autism-Asperger's spectrum, and prone to feeling persecuted. I'm also overweight, nearsighted, and socially awkward. I've always been sympathetic toward &quot;monsters&quot;, especially ones that don't get much say in the matter. On the other hand, some of my other...&quot;quirks&quot; can come in handy, like how hearing the right topic in a conversation can be like doing a Google search: everything I now about that topic will immediately spring to the front of my mind, often cross-referenced with other, tangentially related facts. This can be helpful, but also a bit off-putting, especially when I feel the overwhelming compulsion to butt into strangers conversations. Perhaps you can see how I take being told that becoming &quot;normal&quot; is the only path to happiness as a personal insult.<br /> <br /> \u200bRight, I think I've exposed enough of my soul for one night, let's move on...<br /> <br /> \u200bI know Transmuting means &quot;turn one thing into another thing&quot;, but I didn't say Transmuting, I said Refining.<br /> <br /> I'm all for having drawbacks, I just think that having 5 of them, all quite severe, that can &quot;stack&quot; with each other, is a bit much, especially since most of them are always &quot;on&quot;, as it were. I've mentioned elsewhere that I'm brainstorming a fansplat that would use a lot of Promethean's mechanics, but would ease up on the drawbacks a little; I've tentatively dubbed the it Diogenean: the Search. Basically the idea is some rare few who have been exposed to the Divine Fire(Redeemed, Alchemists, Demiurges) have found a way to &quot;bottle&quot; it, forming a &quot;Lantern of Diogenes&quot;; like an external Azoth battery. Using the power(s) it conveys would still cause some Promethean-style drawbacks, but only when <i>actively</i> using the power(s). I've been meaning to start a tread about it, but not right now; it is late, and I work tomorrow.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T02:47:02-07:00","id":906290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906179#post906179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, that's not entirely true.</div> </div> </div> </div> Entirely, no. Heavily, yes. Of the three past examples on this board I remember, none of them fundamentally addressed the issues of Wastelands, Disquiet and Torment. Especially the ones that end up saying being on fire is kosher. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason why I wouldn't use most of these variants is that they take a dump on the notion that becoming human is a worthwhile goal. </div> </div> </div> For some people, its not. The standard CofD depictation of mortals comes off as mentally fragile - see something supernatural, you break. There are a million things out there that prey on you. By nature, you have to live in denial, be short sighted, and have no free will. Its a pretty cynical take on humanity, and a lot of people react to that depictation as being an undesirable state of being. And I have to agree - being one of the sheeple is an undesirable state of being. Humanism caries certain assumptions that becoming one of the rank and file of CofD mortals doesn't fulfill. Don't forget that we're supposed to invest in these characters - mentally, emotionally, chonologically. We're supposed to empathize with them. I find the idea of being willfully ignorant and somehow losing memories of my original state of being to be something I can't empathize with.<br /> <br /> And this is where we get into gaming elitism. There are some people on these boards that take any changes to their favorite game to be personal insults. Who the frack cares? No one is going to send the fun police after you for having badwrongfun. You say that its not your cup of tea and move on. If someone wants to play Promethean with a different spin, more power to them. Who are you to tell them what is or is not the right way to have fun with a game? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't mind alternatives; but most of them start with the premise that Promethean's natural themes are stupid. </div> </div> </div> People come up with alternatives because they find the default to be undesirable. I can't help but think this is contradictorial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T05:33:54-07:00","id":906334,"title":"","content":"Like the 3 ChroD games before it I figure alternate rules and systems for Promethean will be covered in the Storytelling chapter. Vampire had a ton of alternate ways to play the game that gets to the heart of the game and lets you do what you want. Since there is a fair number of people expressing problems with Promethean's stuff I figure touching on a few ideas would be kosher.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T08:25:30-07:00","id":906427,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is tone. This is to be quite honest an issue on both sides of the debate. There can be a tendency for the ardently humanist camp to lean on the argument of &quot;You just don't <i>get</i> it, man...&quot; which can come off as more than a little condescending. On the other hand, the way a lot of revisionists seem to approach things is &quot;Lulz, this game sucks but lucky for you nerds I fixed it...&quot; which likewise comes off more than a little condescending.<br /> <br /> By way of personal example, I don't like Mummy. Just cannot bring myself to get into it. Something about it fundamentally does not work for me. What I <i>don't</i> do though is show up to their forum dropping taco-powered trouser-bombs on their game and demanding it be rewritten to suit my specific tastes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T09:44:23-07:00","id":906481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906427#post906427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is tone. This is to be quite honest an issue on both sides of the debate. There can be a tendency for the ardently humanist camp to lean on the argument of &quot;You just don't <i>get</i> it, man...&quot; which can come off as more than a little condescending. On the other hand, the way a lot of revisionists seem to approach things is &quot;Lulz, this game sucks but lucky for you nerds I fixed it...&quot; which likewise comes off more than a little condescending.<br /> <br /> By way of personal example, I don't like Mummy. Just cannot bring myself to get into it. Something about it fundamentally does not work for me. What I <i>don't</i> do though is show up to their forum dropping taco-powered trouser-bombs on their game and demanding it be rewritten to suit my specific tastes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I DEMAND THAT YOU REALIZE ALL THE GREAT AND BEAUTIFUL THINGS ABOUT MUMMY OR I'LL RARBLE GLARBLE AT YOU TIL THE END OF YOUR DAYS!<br /> <br /> But in seriousness, I get people not liking games. I get people changing games they don't like. There are places where that's really cool. I love the shit out of the Chronicler's Guides for this reason.<br /> <br /> The Humanist core driven by the flaws in the Promethean condition is not that place for me.<br /> <br /> And this wouldn't a hard conversation, if it hadn't always been fight since day one.(I cannot stress enough just how much of this has been going on since Promethean came out, or the toll that takes.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T12:14:10-07:00","id":906622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906481#post906481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I DEMAND THAT YOU REALIZE ALL THE GREAT AND BEAUTIFUL THINGS ABOUT MUMMY OR I'LL RARBLE GLARBLE AT YOU TIL THE END OF YOUR DAYS!</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking for myself, at least, I hope this is what I actually come across like when I talk to people about <b>Mummy</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T12:16:36-07:00","id":906623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906622#post906622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking for myself, at least, I hope this is what I actually come across like when I talk to people about <b>Mummy</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I would hope not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T14:23:49-07:00","id":906708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906290#post906290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some people, its not. The standard CofD depictation of mortals comes off as mentally fragile - see something supernatural, you break. There are a million things out there that prey on you. By nature, you have to live in denial, be short sighted, and have no free will. Its a pretty cynical take on humanity, and a lot of people react to that depictation as being an undesirable state of being. And I have to agree - being one of the sheeple is an undesirable state of being. Humanism caries certain assumptions that becoming one of the rank and file of CofD mortals doesn't fulfill. Don't forget that we're supposed to invest in these characters - mentally, emotionally, chonologically. We're supposed to empathize with them. I find the idea of being willfully ignorant and somehow losing memories of my original state of being to be something I can't empathize with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that this wasn't so much of a problem in the first edition, when Integrity breaking points for witnessing the supernatural weren't a thing and Lunacy and the Sleeping Curse weren't supercharged, armor-piercing extensions thereof. That is, humans in the nWoD occasionally had a few problems with the supernatural; but it was nothing compared to what they face in ChroD. It's one of two points of contention that I have with the ChroD developers (the other one being the segregation of the various ephemeral Twilights). <br /> <br /> That said, the Promethean designer's position on this, to my knowledge, has always been that the goal <i>isn't</i> bog-normal humans, but rather cream-of-the-crop humans. With that in mind, my patch-job while waiting for 2e to come out is to restructure the Final Azoth Roll so that amnesia is a failure result (total amnesia for a botch, filtering memories through a \u201cmundanity lens\u201d for a regular failure*) and immunity to \u201cwitness the supernatural\u201d breaking points and all anti-mortal agency-robbing effects (Lunacy, Sleeping Curse, Disquiet, Sybaris, etc.) is a result of a <i>normal</i> success (with an Exceptional Success granting a suitable Redeemed Boon). That is, a successful Redemption results in a human who's made of sterner stuff than your run-of-the-mill ChroD mortal, and doesn't instinctively shrink away when the darkness intrudes. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:gray\">* \u201cmundanity lens\u201d: you remember encounters with the supernatural in general, but reinterpret them as much as possible in mundane terms. It's what <b>Mage</b>'s Sleeping Curse imposes on all Sleepers whenever they witness obvious magic. For the Redeemed who fail their Final Azoth Roll, this results in a sort of swiss-cheese memory: the broad strokes of their former life is still there, and they'll recognize people and places they encountered back then; but they'll forget that they used to be monsters, and will misremember scenes where Transmutations were used, etc.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906290#post906290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is where we get into gaming elitism. There are some people on these boards that take any changes to their favorite game to be personal insults. Who the frack cares? No one is going to send the fun police after you for having badwrongfun. You say that its not your cup of tea and move on. If someone wants to play Promethean with a different spin, more power to them. Who are you to tell them what is or is not the right way to have fun with a game?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll note that I didn't enter this conversation until <i>after</i> someone started tossing around accusations likening the \u201cyou're on fire\u201d camp to mobs with torches and pitchforks. That was a case where it had escalated into <i>actual</i> personal insults, largely unprovoked. He has since apologized, so I will say no more on the subject \u2014 just, this isn't \u201cthe innocent visionaries who just want the freedom to do things their own way are being suppressed by those dastardly purist elitists\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-03-2016, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T14:24:47-07:00","id":906709,"title":"","content":"If I were to use transhumanism as a theme, I'd do it via a Centimanus with good intentions and strange ideas who is searching for the New Dusk. Make of that term what you will.<br /> <br /> Besides, it's not like humanism is a restrictive theme. Anything that people have valued immensely over the course of history is fair game. You don't have to find your answers only in the past, either. Prometheans can learn from visions and divine intercessions just as much as the journals and footprints of their ancestors.<br /> <br /> There is just so much you can explore. And no one said that a Promethean who becomes human has to be average or conform to the local definition of normalcy. They can be revolutionary and remembered for centuries, which is something they cannot achieve as disjointed alchemical forges.<br /> <br /> And no, Prometheans are not a metaphor for this or that marginalized group in real life. To make them so would be an oversimplification that can easily result in unfortunate implications. Any sort of isolation can become the game's focus, be it systemic or individual, cultural or spiritual, you name it. That's the beauty of it: taking all these disparate elements and combining them into a journey that speaks to <b><i>you</i></b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T18:44:25-07:00","id":906878,"title":"","content":"If I were to use transhumanism as a theme I wouldn't change anything. I've always found it funny that everyone says Promethean isn't transhumanist when nearly every promthean is meant to be constantly trying to evolve beyond the limits of their flawed bodies. Promethean's pretty transhumanist, just not for the humans :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T18:51:08-07:00","id":906884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906708#post906708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll note that I didn't enter this conversation until <i>after</i> someone started tossing around accusations likening the \u201cyou're on fire\u201d camp to mobs with torches and pitchforks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not trying to stir the pot, and my apology still stands, but you gotta admit invoking that imagery in a Promethean discussion was at least a <i>little</i> clever...<br /> \u200b<br /> So, any feedback on my Diogenean idea? It would still use a LOT of the same mechanics as Promethean, but with a lighter tone, and a somewhat more... Mage-like focus on truth/knowledge-seeking. Obviously, since Diogenoi would have reduced versions of Promethean drawbacks, their advantages would also be diminished somehow. Seriously, the only wrong answer here is that the whole idea is stupid, and I should give up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T19:08:32-07:00","id":906892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906884#post906884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not trying to stir the pot, and my apology still stands, but you gotta admit invoking that imagery in a Promethean discussion was at least a <i>little</i> clever...<br /> \u200b<br /> So, any feedback on my Diogenean idea? It would still use a LOT of the same mechanics as Promethean, but with a lighter tone, and a somewhat more... Mage-like focus on truth/knowledge-seeking. Obviously, since Diogenoi would have reduced versions of Promethean drawbacks, their advantages would also be diminished somehow. Seriously, the only wrong answer here is that the whole idea is stupid, and I should give up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> I don't want to sound dismissive, but I think you could have Diogeneans as a Proximus lineage connected to the Principle somehow. The Lantern could be like a pseudo-soulstone that is the source of their alchemical powers, and any Disquiet or Wasteland-like effects would be the lineage's Curse. You said it yourself that they seek truth and knowledge, and having Mages as allies will definitely help with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T19:54:54-07:00","id":906911,"title":"","content":"There's a fan-made \u201cSons of the Aether\u201d Lineage that was originally conceived as a Promethean crossover Lineage. Though that was before Demon was even a sparkle in the developers' eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T21:34:36-07:00","id":906954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906892#post906892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lantern could be like a pseudo-soulstone that is the source of their alchemical powers.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sort of like a...Philosopher's Stone? Yeah, I thought about that. Could work. What I've been thinking is that channeling the Divine Fire <i>\u200bM</i><i>arks</i> you, no matter how it comes about.The form that Mark takes might resemble the Disfigurements of Promethean Lineages.The Marks become visible when using certain powers, kind of like how using a strong spell can cause a Mage's Nimbus to flare up.<br /> <br /> Redeemed who become Diogenoi(not all Redeemed do) would retain a shadow/echo of their Lineage's Disfigurements.(Scars for Frankenstein, Gauntness for Osiris, etc.)<br /> <br /> Assuming a Demiurge isn't killed by their creation,(or possibly during the Act, with the Zeky) they can never go back to 100% normal. They have stolen from the gods, and the gods have noticed. Maybe their Mark is similar to what their creation must endure.<br /> <br /> I don't have enough data on Alchemists to say how this would work with them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T21:49:56-07:00","id":906960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906884#post906884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not trying to stir the pot, and my apology still stands, but you gotta admit invoking that imagery in a Promethean discussion was at least a <i>little</i> clever...</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a very clever insult, yes. I did appreciate the creativity. <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906884#post906884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, any feedback on my Diogenean idea? It would still use a LOT of the same mechanics as Promethean, but with a lighter tone, and a somewhat more... Mage-like focus on truth/knowledge-seeking. Obviously, since Diogenoi would have reduced versions of Promethean drawbacks, their advantages would also be diminished somehow. Seriously, the only wrong answer here is that the whole idea is stupid, and I should give up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to see 2e's alchemists before commenting. For all I know, your Lantern of Diogenes might be a valid alchemical preparation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-04-2016, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T03:56:46-07:00","id":907053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=905445#post905445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This brings me to something I've been meaning to ask: What, exactly, do you believe is the core premise of Promethean?</div> </div> </div> </div>That it's better to be whole than powerful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=906002#post906002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, &quot;Angry Villagers&quot; will tell you that NO, you CAN'T accept who/what you ARE, you have to become something/someone ELSE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans are born in the wrong bodies, with the world and its people hating them for it and telling them they shouldn't be. They can leverage that state into power, or they can learn about the identity that's already growing in them, understand it, and finally claim it so completly the world has to listen. The world doesn't tell Prometheans they should be human, it tells them they should be monsters - the Centimani are the ones who conform, the Prometheans are the ones who refuse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And there's the conflict between Humanists and Transhumanist players; the Humanists frequently show up in threads they KNOW are about an idea they don't like, and start ranting about how flawed the idea is. </div> </div> </div>Which is functionally what the transhumanist players are doing about the whole game and whole forum. Mind you, after the thread on non-Iremite mummies I get a bit more how you feel, but... the thing is, there's nothing transhumanist about a concept of beings that were never human becoming ever more powerful. It's not transhuman unless <i>humans</i> can attain it. And I've never seen one of the transhumanist players propose that, which is why they come off more as humans-suck.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:49:31-07:00","id":907847,"title":"","content":"Part of what I'd love to see is to make Disquiet less... outside? Outside is the word I want.<br /> <br /> I want to see Disquiet replaced with some sort of <i>fucking up</i>. I want to see everything go smoothly and well and then...<br /> <br /> Oops.<br /> <br /> Because try as you might, you aren't human <i>yet</i>. You aren't human <i>enough</i>. You're a <i>thing</i> right now - that's why you can't stay the way you are.<br /> <br /> Every shibboleth you fuck up, every faux pas that you take, every slip that reveals how alien you are... that's the pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> But then again, I apparently haet Promethean and everything it stands for, think everyone that likes it is totally dumb, and am standing by with the torches and pitchforks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T15:28:46-07:00","id":907928,"title":"","content":"Umm, we <i>just</i> got this topic back into the realm of civility. Did you really have to include that last paragraph? <br /> <br /> As to your main point, I'd be interested to see how something like that might work. Certainly, it would cut down on the \u201cPrometheans are unfairly shat upon by the world\u201d impression that many have if torches and pitchforks only came out after a Created royally screwed up. At the same time, I'd still want this \u201cInside\u201d Disquiet to be enough of a thing that even a Promethean on the doorsteps of the New Dawn aren't exempt from the complications it brings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T18:30:54-07:00","id":908026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=907847#post907847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then again, I apparently haet Promethean and everything it stands for, think everyone that likes it is totally dumb, and am standing by with the torches and pitchforks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The irony on me saying the following is not lost on me:<br /> <br /> Not. Helping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T19:08:30-07:00","id":908039,"title":"","content":"So, I was struck by lighting(metaphorically, of course) on my way to work yesterday, and now I have a hack that might satisfy BOTH camps: What if Disquiet and Wasteland were tied to Pilgrimage, in a manner similar to how Humanity effects certain Banes in Vampire? That way, there is a mechanical benefit to pursuing the Pilgrimage, even for a player who doesn't find becoming human a worthwhile endgame. The higher your Pilgrimage, the slower your Disquiet/Wasteland spread. One of the most frustrating things about the game, at least in the eyes of my gaming group, is that the best way to learn about something is to spend time around it, but the RAW are built around PUNISHING you for trying. I thing that's another reason I wanted to houserule the shit out of P:tC; it's damn near unplayable at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T21:45:10-07:00","id":908122,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm missing something here, but isn't Wasteland as a result of the character's own actions <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/disquiet-and-the-wasteland-everything-and-everyone-hates-you/\" target=\"_blank\">exactly what 2e is doing</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T00:06:37-07:00","id":908185,"title":"","content":"In case you missed it, this is why the transhumanism arguments rankle the forumites immediately: it ALWAYS turns into a fight. Never mind the merits of the argument. Half of it is Promethean grognardism, as the regulars here are in love with a game rejected by most others. It's not that we're blind to its flaws, or we don't houserule the crap out of the game when we're lucky enough to get a game going. It's that we love it for its core conceits that humanity is worthy, that we can overcome bad beginnings, and that no one can define you but yourself. Transhumanism finds fault with human limitations, assumes that we<i> are </i>the bad beginning, and dismisses detractors as shortsighted Luddites. Maybe that's not fair, but it's an argument we've been having on this site and the old one for ten years now, and it's just exhausting.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry that we all have to deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T05:41:57-07:00","id":908277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=908122#post908122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm missing something here, but isn't Wasteland as a result of the character's own actions <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/disquiet-and-the-wasteland-everything-and-everyone-hates-you/\" target=\"_blank\">exactly what 2e is doing</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that was a timely reminder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=907847#post907847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to see Disquiet replaced with some sort of <i>fucking up</i>. I want to see everything go smoothly and well and then...</div> </div> </div> </div>In this vein, perhaps we can add to the list of reasons above, that a Wasteland forms/spreads, or Disquiet kicks up a notch, every time a Promethean experiences Torment, ie their inner fire raging out of control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=908039#post908039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Disquiet and Wasteland were tied to Pilgrimage, in a manner similar to how Humanity effects certain Banes in Vampire? That way, there is a mechanical benefit to pursuing the Pilgrimage, even for a player who doesn't find becoming human a worthwhile endgame.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same thing is happening with Transmutations (mastering Roles gives you access to a wider range of a given Transmutation's abilities), so that's a worthwhile approach. Perhaps, when circumstances dictate that Disquiet or the Wasteland might kick up a notch, the result is determined by an opposed roll of Azoth vs Pilgrimmage - the more powerful you are, the more likely things are to get worse - the more whole you are, the less likely.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T09:30:23-07:00","id":908385,"title":"","content":"You know, to get back on topic, I'm working on a major rules/theme/setting hack of Promethean 2e and one of the things I'm working on is a new Disquiet. <br /> <br /> My main premise is to reverse it: Disquiet takes its biggest toll on first impressions and diminishes as the person in question gets to know the Promethean better, to represent the fact that, while promeatheans may be unusual and disconcerting and often invoke instinctive discomfort in people, people can learn to overcome this through repeated contact with the Promethean/social milestones. Still not sure how to write it up mechanically, but once 2e is out I'll pick it up and go to work on the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T12:19:59-07:00","id":909359,"title":"","content":"Not to start up the arguments again, but the whole &quot;the New Dawn is about rejecting what makes you different so you can conform and be like everyone else&quot; argument has never really borne out for me, at least in the text. My reading of why Prometheans want the New Dawn is much more about &quot;I just want to have what everyone else gets to take for granted, even if I have to work way harder than I should.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe it's just because I can relate to that sentiment, being disabled. I dunno. I don't hate myself, or what I am, but I do recognize that 99% of people don't have to live with the drawbacks and complications I do. If somebody offered me a miracle cure that actually worked, I'd take it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T17:36:39-07:00","id":909629,"title":"","content":"If we're going to talk about this comparison, I need to talk about some of the &quot;whys&quot; in how Promethean not only hooked me into ChroD, but helped me as a person. I won't bore you with the whole story, I'll try and keep it Reader's Digest, but keep in mind when I get to the end that this means some of my explanation will feel a little out of left field.<br /> <br /> A very significant portion of my young life is marked by being alone. I grew up in El Paso, Texas, as a white, upper middle class, geeky scrawny kid in an area and school district filled with poor Hispanic farm-workers and their kids who had to live with the problems-in my elementary school, I was one of three white people, the other being my brother and the nurse, to give a proper sense of scale. I had a target on my back for most of my life for reasons I didn't comprehend 'til I was an adult, and I had very few friends. And then I moved to Colorado, to a school with an noticeable uptick in black population(even with an upswing in financial positioning, though I was still upper to their middle-class), and every trick I had learned for just getting by didn't work here-you couldn't fight the biggest, baddest mofo and earn respect that way, no one wanted to actually fight, and got mad if you did, and verbal sparring was less creative. Even after I got a stable friend base, larger than I had before, most of my friends went to a different school. I spent a good portion of my youth hating people, because the majority just never gave me a chance, and I never once thought why that might have been the case. I just let it reinforce my bitterness towards people.<br /> <br /> I wanted in though, so badly. Even when I lied to myself about it, I wanted in. I wanted to belong. Promethean made me recognize how the pain and lumps of isolation made joining in all the more beautiful, but it's main effect was retroactive, really coming to life on my mission.<br /> <br /> See, on my mission, I became a rock star in our little community. And sure, a lot of that came from the fact that I was a brilliant-but-lazy missionary who knew scriptures, modern prophet speakings, Meso-American archaeology, some of the science of genetic tracing, Judaic symbolism, and more(basically, I was a genius). But honestly, while I didn't actually change who I was a missionary, that being a tabletop/anime nerd who knew way too much about the occult, the mission and how it let me understand people and open up as a response to this understanding of people is the key reason. With the effects of my mission, I connected to others a lot more. With myself, I was a unique, interesting, strange, and bold character. I didn't have to change, I just had to connect. And honestly, that's been the way it's been ever since. I've never had to stray from who I was unless I chose to, but as I learn to connect and understand those around me, I live a happier life, and I'm much more in than I was previously, while still being my own self.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing about Prometheans-they start off with less than I have. They don't have a personhood to start with-that's something that they have to build and develop. But Promethean, talking about people, never says &quot;Give up who you are to fit in&quot;. It's about how taking what good there is and adding to it. It's about how it can be hard to feel at home in your own skin and how there are various forces that can make it very easy for people to ostracize you. It's about how no one really starts with the ability to know how to connect with our fellows in humanity, how to make friends and lovers and all this jazz. Promethean isn't about an abandonment of self, it's about a settling of self, of learning who you are and how to connect to other people, of learning who they are and how to let their lives matter to you, to stop being the outsider and to bring your unique self in, while still building your unique self.<br /> <br /> I don't see the angle of Promethean telling people to conform, outside of the normal success stripping them of their memory(Which, I admit, was always weird). Connection isn't conformity. To be in, to have actually meaningful relationships, doesn't mean to be like everyone else-often times, that just pushes more people away, in the deep senses.<br /> <br /> So, no, I don't agree with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T21:55:54-07:00","id":909831,"title":"","content":"read the title and thought the answer is obviously &quot;Dasquiet&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T18:26:40-07:00","id":910457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=908122#post908122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm missing something here, but isn't Wasteland as a result of the character's own actions <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/disquiet-and-the-wasteland-everything-and-everyone-hates-you/\" target=\"_blank\">exactly what 2e is doing</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHadn't seen that. Thank you for making me aware of it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T00:25:31-07:00","id":910607,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=909629#post909629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're going to talk about this comparison, I need to talk about some of the &quot;whys&quot; in how Promethean not only hooked me into ChroD, but helped me as a person. I won't bore you with the whole story, I'll try and keep it Reader's Digest, but keep in mind when I get to the end that this means some of my explanation will feel a little out of left field.<br /> <br /> A very significant portion of my young life is marked by being alone. I grew up in El Paso, Texas, as a white, upper middle class, geeky scrawny kid in an area and school district filled with poor Hispanic farm-workers and their kids who had to live with the problems-in my elementary school, I was one of three white people, the other being my brother and the nurse, to give a proper sense of scale. I had a target on my back for most of my life for reasons I didn't comprehend 'til I was an adult, and I had very few friends. And then I moved to Colorado, to a school with an noticeable uptick in black population(even with an upswing in financial positioning, though I was still upper to their middle-class), and every trick I had learned for just getting by didn't work here-you couldn't fight the biggest, baddest mofo and earn respect that way, no one wanted to actually fight, and got mad if you did, and verbal sparring was less creative. Even after I got a stable friend base, larger than I had before, most of my friends went to a different school. I spent a good portion of my youth hating people, because the majority just never gave me a chance, and I never once thought why that might have been the case. I just let it reinforce my bitterness towards people.<br /> <br /> I wanted in though, so badly. Even when I lied to myself about it, I wanted in. I wanted to belong. Promethean made me recognize how the pain and lumps of isolation made joining in all the more beautiful, but it's main effect was retroactive, really coming to life on my mission.<br /> <br /> See, on my mission, I became a rock star in our little community. And sure, a lot of that came from the fact that I was a brilliant-but-lazy missionary who knew scriptures, modern prophet speakings, Meso-American archaeology, some of the science of genetic tracing, Judaic symbolism, and more(basically, I was a genius). But honestly, while I didn't actually change who I was a missionary, that being a tabletop/anime nerd who knew way too much about the occult, the mission and how it let me understand people and open up as a response to this understanding of people is the key reason. With the effects of my mission, I connected to others a lot more. With myself, I was a unique, interesting, strange, and bold character. I didn't have to change, I just had to connect. And honestly, that's been the way it's been ever since. I've never had to stray from who I was unless I chose to, but as I learn to connect and understand those around me, I live a happier life, and I'm much more in than I was previously, while still being my own self.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing about Prometheans-they start off with less than I have. They don't have a personhood to start with-that's something that they have to build and develop. But Promethean, talking about people, never says &quot;Give up who you are to fit in&quot;. It's about how taking what good there is and adding to it. It's about how it can be hard to feel at home in your own skin and how there are various forces that can make it very easy for people to ostracize you. It's about how no one really starts with the ability to know how to connect with our fellows in humanity, how to make friends and lovers and all this jazz. Promethean isn't about an abandonment of self, it's about a settling of self, of learning who you are and how to connect to other people, of learning who they are and how to let their lives matter to you, to stop being the outsider and to bring your unique self in, while still building your unique self.<br /> <br /> I don't see the angle of Promethean telling people to conform, outside of the normal success stripping them of their memory(Which, I admit, was always weird). Connection isn't conformity. To be in, to have actually meaningful relationships, doesn't mean to be like everyone else-often times, that just pushes more people away, in the deep senses.<br /> <br /> So, no, I don't agree with you.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200bWow, Arts, it's almost eerie how parts of your story parallel my own! A few more details: Upper middle-class, Multi-Ethnic,(I sometimes compare myself to a Panda; White, Black and Asian) so instead of fitting in with ALL ethnic groups, I don't fit in with ANY.(I'm frequently mistaken for Puerto Rican, but I'm not even a little Hispanic, and don't speak the language.) A high I.Q., but not much focus(Dyslexic, possible ADD.) or ambition. Despite a talent for mimicking accents/dialects/speech patterns, I can still find it hard to get people to understand me... which I may sometimes interpret as mental deficiency on THEIR part. I was raised as one of Jehovah's Witnesses,(a faith that's often misunderstood) so my interested in things of an occult nature made me an outcast even to my own relatives. I guess for me, it's just more interesting to see the Outsider teach the &quot;In&quot; people that being different can be good. Don't get me wrong, I cheer for Pinocchio to get his wish, and I love stories about humanity rising to it's full potential, but &quot;normal&quot; people bore me on a good day, and disgust me on bad ones. (I think maybe the disgust stems from disappointment?) When the mediocre is favored over the exceptional, that's when I think &quot;if that's what it means to be human, count me out.&quot; So, yeah, I would appreciate an alternative in which &quot;standing out&quot; is as valid an end goal as &quot;fitting in&quot;. So for me, finding a &quot;Human+&quot; option is very appealing. Oh, you may have noticed how my posts can seem to jump around from topic to topic a little? Not sure what the diagnosis is for that, ADD, maybe? Sometime it's like I skip a page or two ahead in the &quot;script&quot; of a conversation. But for all the weirdness in my thought patterns, I wouldn't want a &quot;cure&quot;. Because &quot;normal&quot; bores me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 06-09-2016, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T06:58:02-07:00","id":910745,"title":"","content":"The Pilgrimage is a quest for <i>identity</i>, not conformity. Prometheans aren't just different, they're fundamentally <i>broken</i>, and humanity is their <i>reward</i> for fixing themselves. It's not about shedding your uniqueness and dissolving into the grey mass of boring nobodies, it's about finding your true self and proclaiming it with such certainty that the universe can't help but agree.<br /> <br /> Superpowers aren't the thing that make Prometheans unique, they're just a function of their unnatural bodies. This is not who - not what, who - Prometheans really are, it's just a chrysalis of a real person that both carries the Promethean through the metamorphosis and holds her back along the way. Prometheans begin their existence as nonpersons - not because of their powers or their bodies or the effect they have on others, but because they lack identity - they have no name by which others would know them, they have no memories, no experiences affecting their personality, none of the things that make a person. The goal is not to shed your superpowers so that others will accept you, but to experience new things, create new memories, build connections, find your true self so that others <i>can </i>accept you. The metamorphosis of the body is just the final step, and by the time you make it, you shouldn't feel any sense of loss, because you lose nothing of value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T10:21:01-07:00","id":910922,"title":"","content":"I feel as though I fall somewhere in between both sides of the argument. I am a purist at heart, and typically the themes of the CofD resonate with me. I believe from the developer's standpoint, Promethean is a game about being abandoned, misunderstood, struggling to find a place to belong, to truly become human. Becoming human isn't synonymous with being normal. Sure, it isn't about cool powers, righting wrongs, or transforming into a legend. It is instead finding love, compassion, community, and kinship. These themes run deep in both the setting of the game and the mechanics, and many of the fans find them not only appealing, but tantamount to the experience of Promethean.<br /> <br /> Now, that being said...I don't see why you can't twist and tweak to get a different feel from the game. As some have pointed out, your feel will be very different than what was intended by the developers, and you know what, that is perfectly fine. It is ultimately your gaming table, with your stories to tell and act out. Much like poetry, it can be open to interpretation. The way one runs their game does not invalidate the way another does and so on. I encourage creativity. As long as neither disparage the other, we are all better for it in the end. <br /> <br /> If the rules for Disquiet and/or Wastelands aren't working out for your idea of the hero game, perhaps just slice them away? I can see that if you are using the idea of created beings who are becoming bastions of light in a world of darkness things like alienation, rejection, and violence toward the burgeoning champion might be clumsy to your theme. Maybe even allow them to creep in when the hero doesn't pursue loftier ideals? That could be interesting in a CofD kind of way. Heroes who are forced to do good by a cosmic force...or else. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11942-the13thghost","name":"The13thGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T11:23:23-07:00","id":910979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=910607#post910607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Don't get me wrong, I cheer for Pinocchio to get his wish, and I love stories about humanity rising to it's full potential, but &quot;normal&quot; people bore me on a good day, and disgust me on bad ones. (I think maybe the disgust stems from disappointment?) When the mediocre is favored over the exceptional, that's when I think &quot;if that's what it means to be human, count me out.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>1) No, I don't think you and I have similar stories.<br /> <br /> 2) The quoted bothers me. People who are familiar with my affinity for Lost will not be surprised.<br /> <br /> See, Normal people <i>amaze me</i> now. I <i>get</i> them now, and I am in awe of how they handle their lives and become who they are, how they got there, where they'll go. There's a simple power and beauty to the lives of the ordinary that makes every fight for them, for their defense and their progression, <i>worth it</i>. And I think a large part of it comes from an acknowledgement it took me years to accept:<br /> <br /> 3) I am not extraordinary. I am not special.<br /> <br /> I mean, don't get me wrong. I am. I am a storytelling-demigod, a techno-spiritual psycho-shaman who lives beyond his here and now. I'm awesome. But where a lot of people have looked into other's lives and saw sheep, I saw giants. I am not the only burning star in the world. I am not exceptional because, as it turns out, all these crazy, ordinary people we are quick to look down on and disbelieve* are goddesses and demons alike. We are not surrounded by the banal. We are surrounded merely by the oppressed, and despite that, people find their way to fight, or find their time. Not everyone will-but these infinite beings are <i>there already</i>.<br /> <br /> When the &quot;exceptional&quot; is favored over the mediocre, I am forced to conclude, then, that we have become blinded.<br /> <br /> TL;DR, it's a bad idea to tell someone who favors a game where people would trade the wonder of Arcadia for the quieter, sublime beauty of the everyday that the ordinary isn't worth it. Even worse when that person doesn't much trust people who want to &quot;move forward&quot; without an appreciation for that.<br /> <br /> You cannot reach an end if you do not truly know where you start.<br /> <br /> *Yes, even I! If you know my position on Seers, you know I do not believe in people despite their amazing potential! Except I do, for the Pentacle will triumph in the end!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-09-2016, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:08:47-07:00","id":911071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=910979#post910979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot reach an end if you do not truly know where you start.</div> </div> </div> </div>A follow-up to this point from as near to an informed Watsonian on-the-ground perspective as can be produced by a nonfictional character, with no presented stake in the intrinsic worth of humanity save as a contrasting point:<br /> <br /> A lot of people seem to be under the impression that Prometheans carrying a concentration of the Divine Fire around with them is somehow not part of the problem the Pilgrimage attempts to resolve \u2014 is not a reflection of the problem common to most if not all of the magical frameworks that gameline-level splats tend to base their abilities on.<br /> <br /> And I get the appeal of thinking that your superpowers are just tools that your character has at their disposal, because lord knows it's easy to strip them of the wider context in which they operate, but hey.<br /> <br /> Hey!<br /> <br /> Listen.<br /> <br /> <i>They're trying to eat you.</i><br /> <br /> Go on about humanity being prey animals all you like, but they don't individually have to struggle with being <i>actively consumed by vast paranormal forces</i> on a daily basis as a function of simply existing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-09-2016, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T13:12:01-07:00","id":911076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911071#post911071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A follow-up to this point from as near to an informed Watsonian on-the-ground perspective as can be produced by a nonfictional character:<br /> <br /> A lot of people seem to be under the impression that Prometheans carrying a concentration of the Divine Fire around with them is somehow not part of the problem the Pilgrimage attempts to resolve \u2014 is not a reflection of the problem common to most if not all of the magical frameworks that gameline-level splats tend to base their abilities on.<br /> <br /> And I get the appeal of thinking that your superpowers are just tools that your character has at their disposal, because lord knows it's easy to strip them of the wider context in which they operate, but hey.<br /> <br /> Hey!<br /> <br /> Listen.<br /> <br /> <i>They're trying to eat you.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. Wait. Wait.<br /> <br /> Are you? Could it possibly be? Is the suggestion you're offering, could it possibly be also understood alternatively as...<br /> <br /> I 'unno, &quot;You're on fire&quot; or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:06:47-07:00","id":911217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The13thGhost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=910922#post910922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, that being said...I don't see why you can't twist and tweak to get a different feel from the game. As some have pointed out, your feel will be very different than what was intended by the developers, and you know what, that is perfectly fine. It is ultimately your gaming table, with your stories to tell and act out. Much like poetry, it can be open to interpretation. The way one runs their game does not invalidate the way another does and so on. I encourage creativity. As long as neither disparage the other, we are all better for it in the end.<br /> <br /> If the rules for Disquiet and/or Wastelands aren't working out for your idea of the hero game, perhaps just slice them away? I can see that if you are using the idea of created beings who are becoming bastions of light in a world of darkness things like alienation, rejection, and violence toward the burgeoning champion might be clumsy to your theme. Maybe even allow them to creep in when the hero doesn't pursue loftier ideals? That could be interesting in a CofD kind of way. Heroes who are forced to do good by a cosmic force...or else.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bTHIS. And furthermore, I still can't quite wrap my head around why some players insist that a game about creatures <b>cobbled</b> together from different people's corpses, and animated by Alchemy(a word synonymous with <b>change</b>) can't be <b>dismantled, reassembled</b>, and generally <b>altered</b> to suit someone else's needs. But this is all still <b><u><i>WAY</i></u></b> off topic from what this thread was started for.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T16:18:13-07:00","id":911224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911217#post911217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And furthermore, I still can't quite wrap my head around why some players insist that a game about creatures <b>cobbled</b> together from different people's corpses, and animated by Alchemy(a word synonymous with <b>change</b>) can't be <b>dismantled, reassembled</b>, and generally <b>altered</b> to suit someone else's needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>If, after all the discussion that's gone on, you <i>still</i> think <i>that</i> is the point of contention, despite several explicit statements of what the point of contention generally is, you haven't been paying attention.<br /> <br /> This game had one of the shortest 1e material lists in the franchise and it had an entire book dedicated to presenting weird stuff that didn't fit the baseline described in the corebook. <i>Nobody is arguing that you can't tweak the game.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-09-2016, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T17:23:57-07:00","id":911286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911217#post911217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this is all still <b><u><i>WAY</i></u></b> off topic from what this thread was started for.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough. Frankly though, I can't think of anything to say about the original topic. I'd <i>like</i> to; but I really can't think of anything that could reasonably take Disquiet's place without essentially being conceptually equivalent to Disquiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:39:35-07:00","id":911333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911224#post911224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Nobody is arguing that you can't tweak the game.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCould've fooled me. &quot;You're missing the point!!!&quot; seems to happen within the first 3 posts of any Hack/Houserule/Homebrew thread. Even though those posters have NO authority to tell anyone what to do or not do, they still disrupt the conversation, and that makes it harder for anyone to use these forums, which are meant to be for ALL players, to discuss the weird options.<br /> <br /> BTW, what book are you talking about? I only have the core; since I can't find anyone to play it with, I see no point in buying supplemental material.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:10:58-07:00","id":911366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911333#post911333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could've fooled me. \u201cYou're missing the point!!!\u201d seems to happen within the first 3 posts of any Hack/Houserule/Homebrew thread.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not <i>any</i> Back/Houserule/Homebrew thread; just the ones that involve downplaying a Promethean's downsides or trivializing the quest for Mortality. And such threads arguably <i>are</i> missing the point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911333#post911333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even though those posters have NO authority to tell anyone what to do or not do, they still disrupt the conversation, and that makes it harder for anyone to use these forums, which are meant to be for ALL players, to discuss the weird options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Conversely, lashing out at them when the most they've done has been to suggest an alternate venue likewise disrupts the conversation. One such post to that effect derailed this entire thread early on. <br /> <br /> Also, I can't recall the last time any of them has tried to tell anyone what to do or not do. They have occasionally been guilty of threadcrapping; and when that happens, there's a \u201cFlag\u201d button that you can use to report abuse. But beyond that? There's no more of a tendency to squelch a system hacker's free speech than there is a tendency to squelch <i>their</i> free speech by trying to tell them that they can't post in system hack topics. It's an unfortunate fact that a certain amount of walking on eggshells is necessary on this forum, since there are sore spots all around. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911333#post911333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW, what book are you talking about? I only have the core; since I can't find anyone to play it with, I see no point in buying supplemental material.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Magnum Opus</b>. A large number of the hacks from that book ended up making their way into PtC2e in one way or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-09-2016, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:45:14-07:00","id":911427,"title":"","content":"One thing I'd like to point out:<br /> <br /> CoyoteChosen has not responded to this thread. Like. At all.<br /> <br /> Now it's possible he got intimidated away. It's also possible that he was satisfied, in some form or fashion, by the answers given here. It had been a few days since the last post that involved him before someone else has taken up the reins of this thread and has kept it going in all it's train-wrecky magnificence.<br /> <br /> Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T21:21:03-07:00","id":911435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911366#post911366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Magnum Opus</b>. A large number of the hacks from that book ended up making their way into PtC2e in one way or another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! <br /> <br /> \u200bRegarding your other point, downplaying/removing the downsides is pretty much the only option I can see in order to make the game appealing to player outside it's existing masochist/emo/niche fanbase. Seriously, the ONE person in my group who even considered P:tC lost interest as soon as he looked past the surface.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn a completely different note; I feel like there was another way to go with the inspirational material. Again, I know jack shit about the Ulgan myth, but 3 out of the other 4 Lineages are based on love stories.(at least that's the motive for the resurrection attempt) With that in mind, has anyone considered a hack based around Demiurges as would be necromancers, trying to overcome Death? I feel like a chronicle about trying to come to terms with Promethean's drawbacks, but starting from the point of a &quot;Stolen Life&quot;(as opposed to a blank slate) might be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T21:52:07-07:00","id":911450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911435#post911435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bRegarding your other point, downplaying/removing the downsides is pretty much the only option I can see in order to make the game appealing to player outside it's existing<b><span style=\"color:#000000\">masochist/emo/niche fanbase</span></b>. Seriously, the ONE person in my group who even considered P:tC lost interest as soon as he looked past the surface.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">You might want to be a bit less of a dick when describing other fans/players of the game. This is clearly a violation of rule #1 of the forum, I've let some earlier comments slide but enough is enough. This is an official warning, knock it off or a suspension will be issued. This goes for everyone, not just Mangle.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T22:35:50-07:00","id":911469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911435#post911435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911435#post911435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bRegarding your other point, downplaying/removing the downsides is pretty much the only option I can see in order to make the game appealing to player outside it's existing fanbase. Seriously, the ONE person in my group who even considered P:tC lost interest as soon as he looked past the surface.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why 2e <i>has</i> downplayed the downsides. In 2e, Disquiet never progresses beyond the first stage unless you're in a Wasteland; and it takes considerably more to start a Wasteland than it did in 1e: merely hanging around an area isn't enough to trigger it anymore. I don't think that Torment has been downplayed; but then, I haven't heard much in the way of complaints that Torment is too severe. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911435#post911435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a completely different note; I feel like there was another way to go with the inspirational material. Again, I know jack shit about the Ulgan myth, but 3 out of the other 4 Lineages are based on love stories.(at least that's the motive for the resurrection attempt) With that in mind, has anyone considered a hack based around Demiurges as would be necromancers, trying to overcome Death? I feel like a chronicle about trying to come to terms with Promethean's drawbacks, but starting from the point of a \u201cStolen Life\u201d (as opposed to a blank slate) might be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing that 2e is doing that 1e largely avoided is that demiurges are much more common. Where 1e went with the notion that nearly every Promethean had been created by another Promethean, 2e plays up the story potentials of Prometheans with human \u201cparents\u201d. They're <i>still</i> \u201cblank slates\u201d (unless you take the Residual Memory Merit); but they're potentially \u201cstolen lives\u201d too, if the Promethean is the result of an attempt to resurrect a dead loved one. <br /> <br /> That said, let me propose a hack: an Advanced Merit for Residual Memory. In addition to the skill dice that Residual Memory grants, the Promethean usually has access to the memories of whoever donated its brain. Rolls to recall events from the previous life generally provide factual information, but in a way that feels artificial: it's like watching a scene in sepiatone rather than being immersed in the scene. In particular, there's usually no emotional content, nor any internal monologue: the memory reveals what the former person experienced, but not what she thought or felt about it. <br /> <br /> Alternately, the thoughts and feelings <i>are</i> available to the Promethean; but they tend to build Torment, as the Promethean isn't properly equipped to process human emotions. <br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T00:00:47-07:00","id":911505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911469#post911469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're welcome.<br /> <br /> This is why 2e <i>has</i> downplayed the downsides. In 2e, Disquiet never progresses beyond the first stage unless you're in a Wasteland; and it takes considerably more to start a Wasteland than it did in 1e: merely hanging around an area isn't enough to trigger it anymore. I don't think that Torment has been downplayed; but then, I haven't heard much in the way of complaints that Torment is too severe.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne thing that 2e is doing that 1e largely avoided is that demiurges are much more common. Where 1e went with the notion that nearly every Promethean had been created by another Promethean, 2e plays up the story potentials of Prometheans with human \u201cparents\u201d. They're <i>still</i> \u201cblank slates\u201d (unless you take the Residual Memory Merit); but they're potentially \u201cstolen lives\u201d too, if the Promethean is the result of an attempt to resurrect a dead loved one.<br /> <br /> That said, let me propose a hack: an Advanced Merit for Residual Memory. In addition to the skill dice that Residual Memory grants, the Promethean usually has access to the memories of whoever donated its brain. Rolls to recall events from the previous life generally provide factual information, but in a way that feels artificial: it's like watching a scene in sepiatone rather than being immersed in the scene. In particular, there's usually no emotional content, nor any internal monologue: the memory reveals what the former person experienced, but not what she thought or felt about it.<br /> <br /> Alternately, the thoughts and feelings <i>are</i> available to the Promethean; but they tend to build Torment, as the Promethean isn't properly equipped to process human emotions.<br /> <br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bNOW we're getting somewhere! This could make it a LOT easier for me to sell my group on Promethean. That reminds me; I had an idea I posted on the old forums, under a different name: What would happen if a ghost took possession of the Promethean that was made from their corpse? And stranger still, continued the Pilgrimage like that? Who would they be upon reaching the New Dawn?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T05:33:13-07:00","id":912197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911076#post911076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you? Could it possibly be? Is the suggestion you're offering, could it possibly be also understood alternatively as...<br /> <br /> I 'unno, &quot;You're on fire&quot; or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rather than fire, I've been wondering about the metaphor of an explosive chemical reaction. Such a reaction is destructive to its components and potentially the vessel it's held in (Torment), not to mention its surroundings (Wasteland), and the people around it (Disquiet). But it's also energetic (Azoth and Transmutations). And while chemical reactions are usually over quickly, Prometheans are somehow stuck halfway through them. But chemical reactions also have a natural direction they're going in (Mortality). And if you're careful, you can analyse the components in the reaction, figure out what they are, and so more specifically what they &quot;trying&quot; to be (Pilgrimmage, and in 2nd Ed the connection between Roles and Transmutations). And maybe induce the reaction to finish (New Dawn). But chemical reactions tend to produce results that are less energetic than the components going in (hence loss of powers and weaknesses, because they're the same thing).<br /> <br /> How this would relate to an alternative to Disquiet... barring the Azoth vs Pilgrimmage roll I suggested earlier. What if the power inherent in Transmutations is too much for others? Using a Transmutation on a person - no matter how otherwise harmless, or even benign, it might be - risks inducing a lasting sickness that gets worse at roughly the rate of a Wasteland spread? That would preserve the &quot;powers and weaknesses are the same thing&quot; element - since heroic Prometheans would no doubt regard making people ill as a weakness (that's not snark btw) - and encourage Prometheans to be careful about whom-on, when, and why they use their powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911435#post911435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a completely different note; I feel like there was another way to go with the inspirational material. Again, I know jack shit about the Ulgan myth, but 3 out of the other 4 Lineages are based on love stories.(at least that's the motive for the resurrection attempt) With that in mind, has anyone considered a hack based around Demiurges as would be necromancers, trying to overcome Death? I feel like a chronicle about trying to come to terms with Promethean's drawbacks, but starting from the point of a &quot;Stolen Life&quot;(as opposed to a blank slate) might be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember too that the Ulgan have an alterate origin myth based on Orpheus - they have Orpheus as the progenitor, which is more in keeping with their shamanic selves, but from this perspective, Orpheus could be the demiurge and Euridice the progenitor.<br /> <br /> On the subject of ghosts, as of the 2nd Edition, Prometheans have to die at least once before the New Dawn. During this they visit the Underworld and encounter ghosts. As soon as we heard this, a lot of us immediately jumped to the ghosts of those who made up their bodies. For the take you're talking about here, perhaps they encounter the ghost of their body's donor (more likely to be just one in this version, it seems, if resurrection was the goal), and justify their use of it. If the ghost accepts them, perhaps their weaknesses are muted to an extent - such as a cap on how much Azoth can be counted to their severity - as the ghost's blessing makes their life more true and whole (conversely, if the ghost violently rejects the Promethean, the weaknesses might be exacerbated). (One question here might be why the Promethean should have to justify themselves to the ghost, to which the answer is, you're free to present that argument to the ghost and see how far it gets you).<br /> <br /> I don't think that would work for Prometheans in the canon game (I can't see why the ghost's attitude would make any difference to the effects of the Divine Fire), but presumably in the necromantic version, the Prometheans would be animated by something more chthonic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911469#post911469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, let me propose a hack: an Advanced Merit for Residual Memory. In addition to the skill dice that Residual Memory grants, the Promethean usually has access to the memories of whoever donated its brain. Rolls to recall events from the previous life generally provide factual information, but in a way that feels artificial: it's like watching a scene in sepiatone rather than being immersed in the scene. In particular, there's usually no emotional content, nor any internal monologue: the memory reveals what the former person experienced, but not what she thought or felt about it.<br /> <br /> Alternately, the thoughts and feelings are available to the Promethean; but they tend to build Torment, as the Promethean isn't properly equipped to process human emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I prefer the second option. Or perhaps the Promethean can choose, and accept the risk in the latter case. Or, if the Promethean masters a Role that was <i>also</i> significant to the donor's life, they either get the emotional content, or it no longer poses a risk.<br /> <br /> To get weirder, it's not the memories of whomever the brain comes from, but whomever the organ associated with their Humour comes from (so liver for the Frankensteins, lungs for the Tammuz, gall-bladder for the Osirians, and spleen for the Galateids). Brain or heart might work for the Extemporae (though they are more likely to come from a single body in any case, making it moot).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T11:04:37-07:00","id":912322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=911505#post911505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bNOW we're getting somewhere! This could make it a LOT easier for me to sell my group on Promethean. That reminds me; I had an idea I posted on the old forums, under a different name: What would happen if a ghost took possession of the Promethean that was made from their corpse? And stranger still, continued the Pilgrimage like that? Who would they be upon reaching the New Dawn?</div> </div> </div> </div> Possession doesn't change you on a deep level, that's more like Claiming. However, if the ghost turns the Promethean into a Fetter and Urges them frequently over a long period, the Promethean might suffer an increase in a Humour associated with the ghost's personality and the circumstances of their death. If not that, the Promethean might have to take their Pilgrimage in another direction to get rid of the ghost somehow, and learn about humans in the process. &quot;We all have to face death and we all have something we don't want to let go&quot;, and all that.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't like giving Demiurges universal motivations and methods of channeling the Divine Fire. If you want to homebrew a Lineage that deals with ghostly phenomena but not spirits, go ahead, but applying a coat of necromancy to Prometheans as a whole makes them less diverse for little pay-off. <br /> <br /> What did you think of my idea of turning your Diogeneans into a Proximus lineage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T16:41:05-07:00","id":912521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=912322#post912322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Possession doesn't change you on a deep level, that's more like Claiming. However, if the ghost turns the Promethean into a Fetter and Urges them frequently over a long period, the Promethean might suffer an increase in a Humour associated with the ghost's personality and the circumstances of their death. If not that, the Promethean might have to take their Pilgrimage in another direction to get rid of the ghost somehow, and learn about humans in the process. &quot;We all have to face death and we all have something we don't want to let go&quot;, and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bInteresting idea, but what I was thinking was a little different; imagine a ghost driving around the Promethean that was made from their own corpse. Now imagine that ghost is aware of the Promethean condition, and is trying to turn this reanimate body back into a living one, literally trying to take their life back. Would it be possible? If so, who would they be? Would the ghost have cheated death, or would the New Dawn drive them from the body?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, I don't like giving Demiurges universal motivations and methods of channeling the Divine Fire. If you want to homebrew a Lineage that deals with ghostly phenomena but not spirits, go ahead, but applying a coat of necromancy to Prometheans as a whole makes them less diverse for little pay-off. </div> </div> </div> Well, not ALL Demiurges. Dr. Frankenstein was acting out of hubris more than love,(maybe that's part of why his creation{s} are so Wretched?) but the fluff is pretty clear; The mortals call forth the Divine Fire only by acts of passion, desperation, or madness.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What did you think of my idea of turning your Diogeneans into a Proximus lineage? </div> </div> </div> I like the <i>sound</i> of the idea, but TBH, I'm not 100% clear on what a Proximus is. That's a Mage thing, right?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T16:59:46-07:00","id":912529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/900708-idea-alternative-s-to-disquiet?p=912521#post912521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bInteresting idea, but what I was thinking was a little different; imagine a ghost driving around the Promethean that was made from their own corpse. Now imagine that ghost is aware of the Promethean condition, and is trying to turn this reanimate body back into a living one, literally trying to take their life back. Would it be possible? If so, who would they be? Would the ghost have cheated death, or would the New Dawn drive them from the body?<br /> <br /> Well, not ALL Demiurges. Dr. Frankenstein was acting out of hubris more than love,(maybe that's part of why his creation{s} are so Wretched?) but the fluff is pretty clear; The mortals call forth the Divine Fire only by acts of passion, desperation, or madness.<br /> <br /> I like the <i>sound</i> of the idea, but TBH, I'm not 100% clear on what a Proximus is. That's a Mage thing, right?</div> </div> </div> </div> The scenario you are describing for the ghost assumes a lot of things that don't happen often, so there is not an abundance of similar cases that can be used as a baseline. Keep in mind that the great majority of ghosts are not very powerful, and it's hard for them to learn new tricks. I find it more likely that the ghost will be changed in some way by trying to take back their life, rather than the Promethean. After all, it is the Promethean who possesses a raging furnace of transforming power animating them.<br /> <br /> As for what Proximi are, I suggest you take a quick look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11Urxj0z6zvILm6-RAdUWXi5X_M6ppIjQ54H2Cb_prQM/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"><b>this</b></a>. If that doesn't sound independent enough for you, the Diogeneans could be a Path instead of Proximi. Their Ruling Arcana are all but guaranteed to be Prime and Matter. There's more to a Path than that, of course, such as what they perceive when using Mage Sight, what Supernals they can Summon and how their Nimbuses affect people and their surroundings. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}